  <h1 class="mb-5 mt-0 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-base-content sm:text-[2.8rem]">Operator Benchmark</h1>

  <p class="byline">
    By <a href="/authors/alex-rowan/">Alex Rowan</a> ·
    Published {{ publishedAt | readableDate }} · Last updated {{ updatedAt | readableDate }} ·
    <a href="mailto:alex@socialcasinoindex.com">alex@socialcasinoindex.com</a>
  </p>

  <div class="answer-first">
    <span class="af-label">What this is</span>
    <p>This benchmark records what we could verify about each operator we track, and — just as important — what we could not. Every field carries a verification status. Where a partner's terms are not publicly reachable, we say so rather than fill the gap with assumptions.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="partners">Partners</h2>
  <p>These operators hold affiliate agreements with Social Casino Index (see the <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>). Commercial relationships determine which links can earn commission, not which facts appear in the benchmark.</p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="data">
      <caption>Partner player-value terms, September 2026. "Not publicly verified" means we could not confirm the field from a stable first-party source.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Partner</th>
          <th scope="col">Best for</th>
          <th scope="col">Published timing</th>
          <th scope="col">Methods</th>
          <th scope="col">Min redemption</th>
          <th scope="col">Verification</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for op in operators %}
          {% if op.partner %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href="/redemption-times/{{ op.slug }}/">{{ op.name }}</a></th>
            <td>{{ op.bestFor }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.publishedEstimate }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.methods }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.minRedemption }}</td>
            <td><span class="badge {% if op.verificationStatus == 'verified' %}complete{% else %}pending{% endif %}">{{ op.verificationLabel }}</span></td>
          </tr>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="context">Context operators</h2>
  <p>These major operators provide market context and carry no affiliate links on this site.</p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="data">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Operator</th>
          <th scope="col">Best for</th>
          <th scope="col">Published estimate</th>
          <th scope="col">Methods</th>
          <th scope="col">Minimum</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for op in operators %}
          {% if not op.partner %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href="/redemption-times/{{ op.slug }}/">{{ op.name }}</a></th>
            <td>{{ op.bestFor }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.publishedEstimate }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.methods }}</td>
            <td>{{ op.minRedemption }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="methodology">How we verify</h2>
  <p>Each operator's terms and sweepstakes rules are fetched directly, or via a US-located scrape when the operator blocks our region. Fields we cannot confirm from a public document are marked <em>unverified</em> — never filled in from assumption. Verification access dates are recorded in the dataset and updated on re-check.</p>

  <h2 id="sources">Source register</h2>
  <ol class="sources">
    {% for op in operators %}
      {% for s in op.sources %}
      <li><strong>{{ op.name }}</strong> — {{ s.label }}. <a href="{{ s.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ s.url | replace("https://", "") | replace("http://", "") }}</a>. <span class="accessed">Accessed {{ s.accessed | readableDate }}.</span></li>
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

